ed the  failings of the government  his former boss was facing questions in  parliament  i don't think anybody could credibly  accuse this government of being  complacent about the threat that this  virus posed  at any at any point we have worked flat  out  mr speaker but more questions are being  raised and more evidence will be given  as parliament's health  sciences and technology committees  investigate britain's pandemic response  more than 127 thousand people have died  from covid19 so far  an independent inquiry into the  government's handling of the crisis  begins next year crystal gomanson global  news  london india now hit  by a cyclone coming up the natural  disaster happening on top of the covid  disaster  plus a site not seen in three thousand  years  this is the last thing india needs right  now cyclone yaz  slammed into the country's east coast  this morning more than a million people  were forced to flee their homes  a huge tidal surge has turned roads into  rivers and homes  to rubble at least six people are known  to have died  in the storm police in italy have  arrested three people after that cable  car plunged to the ground and killed 14  people  officers say a clamp was used to  intentionally deactivate the emergency  brake on the cable car  it failed to engage when the main cable  snapped the cable car plunged to the  ground and rolled down a steep hill  prosecutors believe the move was a stop  gap measure to avoid shutting down the  attraction for extensive repairs  criminal charges are being considered a  five-year-old boy is the only survivor  he is recovering in the hospital  for the first time in three thousand  years tasmanian  devils are officially back and breeding  on mainland australia  seven tiny joeys were born at this  wildlife sanctuary near sydney  the team from aussie arc has been  working for 10 years to reintroduce the  endangered marsupial to the mainland  they died out on mainland australia  after the arrival  of dingoes  t