ich pushed the lab theory and allowed  conspiracy theories to flourish  and there is significant evidence that  this came from the laboratory  scientists say it's not about laying  blame but answers are important  it's about the origin of this virus and  being able to prevent  future pandemics before they start that  could help contain future outbreaks or  prevent  future mistakes it won't bring back all  that's been lost  or stop the virus that's still raging  around the world  jackson prosko global news washington  got grain next the growing demand for  milk alternatives  the duke and duchess of cambridge have  gone back to their university days in  scotland they went head to head in a  land yachting race at st  andrews where they met and fell in love  20 years ago the royal couple  raced in wind powered go-karts organized  by a charity that helps teenagers who  care for family members  at one point kate's back wheel was  lifted up by the force of the wind  and prince williamwell he claimed he won  there are all kinds of options these  days if you don't or  can't drink cow's milk there's milk made  from soy from  almonds and from oats oat milk has  actually been around for decades but  now it's really taken off and become a  multi-billion dollar product  mike trolley explains why oat milk is  no booming oat milk marketing has  targeted  a certain demographic it's for the next  gen my gen  more specifically gen zed and  millennials and those generations are  not only listening  they've made oat milk the health fad of  the year  oatley the swedish based company that  made milking a note cool  went public last week with a valuation  of 10 billion  u.s numbers like that don't mean much in  coffee shops  here at toronto's wallace espresso it's  all about taste  they steam up really closely to the way  dairy does daniel wallen says his oat  milk orders  have risen sharply over the past three  years and now eclipse soy and almond  as the alternative of choice but the  other thing with oat milk is because i  feel it's so close to dairy milk in  flavor  and texture it's reached a broader  audience it's the same audience that fed  into the plant-based burger boom of  2019.  health is an issue for them but so too  is the environment and oat milk uses far  less land  and has fewer greenhouse gas emissions  than dairy it also takes 628 liters of  water to produce one liter of milk  compared with 371 liters for a liter of  almond milk  and 48 liters for oat milk i think it's  a great  alternative right now until something  else comes along  we've had all sorts of milk that haven't  really stuck but if you think about hemp  milk  it does not taste good so if there's a  product on the market that tastes good  you can put it in your coffee you can  put it on your cereal and it doesn't  feel like you're hard done by  then i think it's more likely to stick  oat milk certainly checks all those  boxes  and that's bringing smiles to canadian  farmers who produce more oats than  anywhere outside the european union an  oat  is certainly growing it was really  kind of the forgotten child in the  prairies for a very long time but  now it's becoming a really sexy  proposition for many farmers sexy  oats why not mike droli global news  toronto  some exciting plans for lunar  exploration were revealed today the  canadian government has put out a  request for proposals to build a robotic  vehicle that could end up  on the moon within the next five years  canada plans to land a lunar rover  on the moon that's the big news today  to achieve that objective the canadian  space agency will be looking for two  canadian companies  to develop concepts for the rover and  science  instruments for the mission  it will have to make it through the  extreme cold and dark of a lunar night  which lasts about two weeks  just the job for canada right there was  just another rare lunar event that  required  less expertise it's called the super  flower blood moon and it was the only  total  lunar eclipse in 2021 it was visible on  the west coast in the early morning  hours  it's a super moon because it's full when  it's at its closest point to the earth  the blood is from the red color that's  the result of the lunar eclipse  and the flower is what a full moon is  called in may  that's global national for this  wednesday i'm donna friesen thanks for  watching hope to see you here again  tomorrow  take care of yourselves bye-bye  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

